From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] svulkan2/openvr: add riscv64 branch

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 build infra detail, out of scope for the comoco-xiao/openvr fork sapien-vulkan-2 pins]

openvr's own CMakeLists.txt picks -DLINUXARM64 only for
CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR=="aarch64" and otherwise -DLINUX64 for any
other 64-bit unix target, so riscv64 silently takes the x86_64-labeled
branch today. openvr_api is linked into svulkan2 but only exercised
with real VR hardware, which none of our runners have, so this is
unlikely to matter in practice -- added anyway for correctness rather
than leaving riscv64 mislabeled as LINUX64 in a dependency we vendor.

We don't control the comoco-xiao/openvr fork directly (it's fetched
fresh via FetchContent at configure time, not vendored in this repo),
so patch cmake/openvr.cmake's FetchContent_Declare to add a
PATCH_COMMAND that rewrites the one line in its CMakeLists.txt right
after the source is populated.

The PATCH_COMMAND's python3 argument has to stay on a single logical
line. FetchContent_Populate's own sub-build still generates a
recursive-make project for this step regardless of the outer build's
generator, and embeds the COMMAND argument verbatim into the
generated CMakeFiles/openvr-populate.dir/build.make recipe; Make
requires every physical line of a recipe to start with a tab, so a
COMMAND argument containing literal, unescaped newlines (the original
version of this patch, wrapped across several lines for readability)
corrupts that generated recipe and fails configure with "build.make:
*** missing separator. Stop." before openvr is even fetched. Using
`\n` as a Python string escape instead of a real newline keeps the
replacement multi-line in the patched CMakeLists.txt without putting
a raw newline byte in the Makefile that generates it.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 3rd_party/sapien-vulkan-2/cmake/openvr.cmake | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/3rd_party/sapien-vulkan-2/cmake/openvr.cmake b/3rd_party/sapien-vulkan-2/cmake/openvr.cmake
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/3rd_party/sapien-vulkan-2/cmake/openvr.cmake
+++ b/3rd_party/sapien-vulkan-2/cmake/openvr.cmake
@@ -5,6 +5,10 @@
     GIT_TAG        v0.0.1
     GIT_SHALLOW TRUE
     GIT_PROGRESS TRUE
+    # Kept on one line: FetchContent_Populate's own sub-build generates a
+    # recursive-make project for this step and embeds this COMMAND verbatim
+    # into its build.make recipe, where a literal newline breaks "missing separator".
+    PATCH_COMMAND python3 -c [[import pathlib; p = pathlib.Path("CMakeLists.txt"); s = p.read_text(); old = 'elseif(PROCESSOR_ARCH MATCHES "64")'; new = 'elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "riscv64")\n      add_definitions(-DLINUXRISCV64)\n    elseif(PROCESSOR_ARCH MATCHES "64")'; assert old in s; p.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1))]]
 )

 # FetchContent_MakeAvailable(openvr)
--
